---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { analyze, DEFAULT_CSS } from '../../lib/audit/model';
import { summaryView, graphView, tableView, detailsView } from '../../lib/audit/views';
import { h, renderToString } from '../../lib/view/h';
import { PERSON_ID, ref } from '../../lib/seo/entities';
import '../../styles/stylesheet-audit.css';

const tool = await getEntry('tools', 'stylesheet-audit');
if (!tool) throw new Error('Missing tools/stylesheet-audit.md');
const result = analyze(DEFAULT_CSS);
if (!result.ok) throw new Error(result.error.message);
const url = new URL('/stylesheet-audit/', Astro.site).href;
const output = [
  summaryView(result.value), graphView(result.value),
  h('div', { 'data-audit-table-slot': true }, tableView(result.value)),
  detailsView(result.value),
].map(renderToString).join('');
const jsonLd = [{
  '@type': 'WebApplication', '@id': `${url}#app`, name: tool.data.title, url,
  description: tool.data.summary, applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any',
  browserRequirements: 'Requires a modern browser. Works without JavaScript as a read-only example.',
  isAccessibleForFree: true, inLanguage: 'en',
  datePublished: tool.data.publishedAt.toISOString().slice(0, 10),
  dateModified: tool.data.updatedAt.toISOString().slice(0, 10),
  keywords: tool.data.keywords.join(', '), offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: 0, priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  author: ref(PERSON_ID),
}];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Stylesheet Audit: CSS specificity, layers and findings"
  description={tool.data.summary}
  path="/stylesheet-audit/"
  og="stylesheet-audit"
  ogAlt={tool.data.ogTitle ?? tool.data.title}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Lab', path: '/' }, { name: tool.data.title, path: '/stylesheet-audit/' }]}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="tool-hero" aria-labelledby="tool-title" data-audit-app>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 id="tool-title">See the shape of your CSS</h1>
      <p class="tool-lead">Stylesheet Audit: follow specificity from the first selector to the last.</p>
      <noscript><p class="notice mt-m">JavaScript is off. This complete worked example will not update.</p></noscript>
      <p class="notice mt-m" data-audit-notice role="status" hidden></p>
      <div class="field mt-l">
        <label class="label" for="audit-css">Your CSS</label>
        <textarea class="input audit-css" id="audit-css" rows="12" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="audit-help" data-audit-css>{DEFAULT_CSS}</textarea>
        <p class="muted mt-s" id="audit-help">Up to 100 KB of UTF-8 CSS; the first 5,000 selectors are reported. Individual selectors retain the engine's 1,000-character limit and nesting expansions its 2,000-character limit. Expanded layer paths are also capped at 100 KB. Share links accept up to 8 KB of CSS.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="prose mt-m">Your CSS is parsed locally, never applied to this page. Imports and resource URLs are never fetched. No analytics or input storage. Nothing is put in the URL until you press Copy link; shared URLs contain the CSS, not an encrypted secret.</p>
      <div class="duel-actions mt-m js-only">
        <button class="button" type="button" data-audit-copy aria-describedby="audit-copy-status">Copy link</button>
        <p class="status" id="audit-copy-status" data-audit-copy-status role="status"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="field mt-s" data-audit-link-wrap hidden>
        <label class="label" for="audit-link">Link to this audit</label>
        <input class="input" id="audit-link" type="text" readonly data-audit-link />
      </div>
      <p class="status mt-s" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-audit-live></p>
      <div class="mt-xl" data-audit-output set:html={output} />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="audit-explainer">
    <div class="wrap stack">
      <h2 id="audit-explainer">A map, not a verdict</h2>
      <p class="prose">A specificity graph shows selector weight in source order. Peaks identify places to review, not guaranteed bugs. A higher-weight rule can resist later rules only when they compete in the same cascade context. Origin, importance and layers are considered before specificity. Read <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Specificity">how specificity fits the cascade</a>.</p>
      <h3>Read the full triple</h3>
      <p class="prose">Specificity compares ID, class and type columns from left to right. The graph caps each column at nine solely for display; sorting and findings use the full triple. A spike here means higher specificity than every available entry in the next ten positions, with at least one following entry. No stylesheet-wide score or grade is assigned.</p>
      <h3>Lower weight deliberately</h3>
      <p class="prose"><code>:where()</code> and its arguments add no specificity. <code>:is()</code>, <code>:not()</code> and <code>:has()</code> use their most specific argument. Nesting uses the maximum weight of the parent selector list, not necessarily the parent that matches. See <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/selectors-4/#specificity-rules">Selectors Level 4</a> and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Nesting/Nesting_and_specificity">nesting and specificity</a>. Removing weight changes the cascade; check the rendered page before applying a suggestion.</p>
      <h3>Give layers a job</h3>
      <p class="prose">Declare a layer order before adding rules. Later layers outrank earlier ones for normal declarations within the same origin; unlayered normal declarations take priority over layered ones. The order reverses for important declarations. Within a parent layer, its own normal declarations outrank its sublayers. See <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@layer">the layer rules</a>.</p>
      <h3>What a pasted stylesheet cannot tell us</h3>
      <p class="prose">This audit does not evaluate media conditions, match selectors against a document, expand imports, or compare property values. Keyframes, font descriptors and unsupported at-rule groups are not selector rules and are reported as excluded. Rules with declarations after nested rules appear as separate declaration runs to preserve source order. Empty rules remain visible. The report is a starting point for review, not a replacement for browser inspection.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  import '../../scripts/stylesheet-audit';
</script>
